 mask←object(State BuildMask)edges;size;rc;hw;props;canvas
⍝ We need this to build a reusable clipping mask for ∇GUI to apply
⍝ The result should be a boolean array of the size of State._pix_size
⍝ The right argument should be either a rectangle-style (4⍴start,size) or a 2-column matrix of polygon points, in 0-origin pixels
⍝ Obvious argument structural errors simply return a Value Error rather than a formal error message

 size←State._pix_size
 :If (1=≢⍴edges)∧4=≢edges                                       ⍝ *** In standard (start,size) rectangular form
     rc←2↑edges ⋄ hw←2↓edges ⋄ mask←size↑(-rc+hw)↑hw⍴1          ⍝ We'll just manually build a simple bit mask

 :ElseIf (2=≢⍴edges)∧(2=¯1↑⍴edges)∧1<≢edges                     ⍝ *** They've given us a polygonal shape - this is more difficult
     canvas←State._Owner⍕⍛,'.',##.Next State._Owner             ⍝ We're going to build a temporary Bitmap here
     canvas←⎕VGET canvas ##.∆WC'Bitmap'('CBits'(size⍴¯1+⌊256*3)) ⍝ We'll use this White space to ask Dyalog to draw our Black polygon for us
     props←StartObj'Poly'
     props,←('LStyle' 5)('LWidth' 0)                            ⍝ Hide the edge itself ⍝? (does this work well enough?)
     props,←('BCol'(3⍴255))('FStyle' 0)('FillCol'(3⍴0))
     props,←⊂'Points'edges
     {}(State NewName canvas)##.∆WC props                       ⍝ Draw their requested polygon
     mask←canvas ##.∆WG'CBits'                                  ⍝ Retrieve the hopefully Black & White pixels to see where it ended up
     mask←0=mask                                                ⍝ Everywhere it was pure Black, that's inside the polygon and is where we want to allow output
     ##.∆EX⍕canvas                                              ⍝ We don't need this any more
 :EndIf
